{
  "id": 501373038,
  "iid": 25595,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "HTTP: add expert warning for whitespace in request-target",
  "description": "## Summary\n\nRFC 9112 §3.2 states that **\"No whitespace is allowed in the request-target.\"**\n\nCurrently, HTTP request-targets containing embedded SP or HTAB characters are dissected without an Expert Info indication. This change validates the extracted request-target for prohibited whitespace and emits `ei_http_request_uri_invalid` when such whitespace is present, while preserving normal dissection of the request.\n\n## Changes\n\n* Validate extracted HTTP request-targets for embedded SP or HTAB characters.\n* Reuse the existing `ei_http_request_uri_invalid` Expert Info for malformed request-target syntax.\n* Leave valid request-targets unchanged.\n* Add a regression capture (`http-tab-request.pcapng`).\n* Add a corresponding HTTP regression test.\n\n## Example\n\nMalformed request:\n\n`GET /foo<TAB>bar HTTP/1.1\nHost: example.com\n`\n\n(`TAB` represents a single HTAB character, `0x09`, embedded between `foo` and `bar`.)\n\nAfter this change:\n\n* `http.request.uri` is still dissected normally.\n* `ei_http_request_uri_invalid` is emitted for the malformed request-target.\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified with:\n\n* `tshark -V` using the new regression capture.\n* `TestDissectHttp::test_http_request_target_whitespace`\n* Full `TestDissectHttp` test suite.\n\nAll tests pass successfully.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-06-29T20:46:53.528Z",
